Adam AI — licensing and scope
=============================

This repository is a genuine GitHub fork of:

    https://github.com/gazijarin/AdamAI

Copyright in the inherited simulation belongs to its original authors,
Gazi Jarin <https://github.com/gazijarin> and
Raiyan Rahman <https://github.com/RaiyanRahman>.

The upstream repository publishes NO licence (`license: null`, no LICENSE file).
Its source is therefore "all rights reserved" by its authors. Nothing in this
repository relicenses that code, and no MIT grant is asserted over it.


WHAT IS LICENSED, AND HOW
-------------------------

Original work created for this fork (Mohammed Unais) is MIT licensed. The full
MIT text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt and applies only to:

    index.html
    assets/css/style.css
    js/site/main.js
    .github/workflows/deploy.yml
    README.md
    NOTICE.md
    LICENSES/**
    docs/**

Not covered by that grant:

    js/simulation/**   inherited from gazijarin/AdamAI and modified; remains
                       under its original authors' copyright
    libraries/**       third-party: p5.js and addons, LGPL-2.1
                       (see libraries/README.md)


WHY THE MIT TEXT IS NOT IN THIS FILE
------------------------------------

GitHub's licence detector reads a root LICENSE file and applies one label to
the whole repository. Putting the MIT text here would make GitHub advertise
this repository as MIT-licensed, which would misrepresent the inherited
simulation. The MIT grant therefore lives in LICENSES/MIT.txt, scoped to the
files listed above, and this file records the split.

If you reuse this project: treat the two halves separately. The interface,
instrumentation, documentation and CI are MIT — use them freely. The simulation
core is not yours or mine to relicense; ask the upstream authors.


